# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15), from the product owner's note of that day on F48 and rule 5 in collab/QUESTIONS.md; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a frame a person gives a window while Arbor is paused, or not running, is its own from then on. An editor and a browser are docked.
# ⌃⌥⎋: both are as they were before Arbor touched them. The person makes the browser smaller and puts it somewhere else. ⌃⌥⎋ again: the arrangement
# is back, as if nothing had happened. But the next time Arbor lets go, the browser goes to where its person put it, not to where it lay before
# it was first docked.
# Reference: F48, F40; issue #3 rule 5.
open Editor 700x500
open Browser 900x600
move 101 100 100 700 500
move 102 300 150 900 600
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
pause
expect at 102 300 150
expect size 102 900x600
move 102 500 300 700 500
resume
expect docked 101
expect docked 102
expect left-of 101 102
pause
expect at 102 500 300
expect size 102 700x500
# Nobody touched the editor.
expect at 101 100 100
expect size 101 700x500
resume
# A window that floats by itself takes that size, where it is.
float 102
expect size 102 700x500
dock 102 right
# The same after a quit, and Float All goes by the same frame.
relaunch quit
expect size 102 700x500
move 102 420 200 640 380
relaunch start
expect docked 102
float-all
expect at 102 420 200
expect size 102 640x380
expect at 101 100 100
expect size 101 700x500
